00:22:44,770 --> 00:22:48,880
says that, you know, choose
truthfulness over helpfulness

491
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:49,460
over here.

492
00:22:49,460 --> 00:22:50,630
So let me see that.

493
00:22:50,630 --> 00:22:51,240
Where is that?

494
00:22:51,240 --> 00:23:00,985

495
00:23:00,985 --> 00:23:01,485
Yeah.

496
00:23:01,485 --> 00:23:04,240

497
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:07,797
So they wanted to prioritize
harmlessness and truthfulness

498
00:23:07,797 --> 00:23:10,130
over helpfulness, but we went
with the other way around.

499
00:23:10,130 --> 00:23:14,050
We said we wanted to prioritize
helpfulness over honesty

500
00:23:14,050 --> 00:23:15,400
or harmlessness because--

501
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:17,410
I mean, we weren't even
focusing on harmlessness

502
00:23:17,410 --> 00:23:19,420
because we just wanted
to get our model

503
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:23,380
to a certain capabilities before
we start thinking about that.

504
00:23:23,380 --> 00:23:26,170
But yeah, this is really
a very good document

505
00:23:26,170 --> 00:23:29,620
and defines what should the
annotator be looking at,

506
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:33,590
and how do they decide when the
model responses are very close,

507
00:23:33,590 --> 00:23:36,980
how do they break those ties?

508
00:23:36,980 --> 00:23:39,890
And for deciding between
what kind of template

509
00:23:39,890 --> 00:23:42,550
should be used for
collecting these annotations,

510
00:23:42,550 --> 00:23:44,300
we started off with
the Anthropic template

